course: dictionary
lesson: 1539
title: Chaff: the part we throw away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chaff is the dry outer case around a grain of wheat. When farmers thresh the wheat, the chaff comes away from the seeds, and the wind blows it off. So chaff is the part nobody wants. «Sort the wheat from the chaff» means keep the good things and throw away the rubbish.
explain: Now look at this sentence: «On the way out the warders chaff him with jokes.» Chaff is a verb here, a doing word. The jokes are the clue. People chaff a friend with jokes to tease them in fun, not to hurt them. The dictionary gives this meaning as old-fashioned, so you will mostly find it in old books.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each one in the sentence. Does «the warders tease him with jokes» make sense? Yes. Does «the warders throw him out with the husks» make sense? No. The context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Chaff is the dry husk around the seeds of grain such as wheat.
fact: Farmers separate the chaff from the seeds when they thresh the grain.
fact: «Chaff» can also mean cut hay or straw, used as animal food.
fact: «Chaff» can mean something useless, as in «sort the wheat from the chaff».
fact: «To chaff someone» is an old-fashioned way to say tease them in fun. Chaff is uncountable as a noun, so you say some chaff, not a chaff.
exercise: «The farmer threshed the wheat, and the light chaff blew away in the wind.» What is the chaff in this sentence? | *The dry husks that come off the grain | A kind of tractor | A flock of birds | A field of tall grass
exercise: Mum says, «Stop chaffing your brother, it is not kind.» What does chaffing mean? | Sorting seeds from husks | Feeding the animals with hay | Cutting straw into short pieces | *Teasing him in fun
exercise: What does the phrase «sort the wheat from the chaff» mean? | Feed the hens in the yard | Blow the dust off the grain | *Keep the good things and throw out the bad | Grow wheat in a big field
test: Farmers mix chaff into the feed for the cows. What is chaff here? | A kind of ploughed field | *Cut hay or straw used as animal food | Sweet, sugary grain | A spade for digging
test: An old story says the wicked are like chaff that the wind drives away. What does this show? | A strong wind that brings rain | *Something worthless that gets swept away | A happy harvest song | A precious thing kept safe
exam: Which sentence uses chaff to mean teasing in fun? | The farm boy filled the barn with chaff | *The warders chaff him with jokes all the way out | The chaff blew off the threshing floor | Dad sorted the wheat from the chaff
